<!--
  RESEARCH CONSENT GATE

  The research deployment's route "/" lands here, not on the module. Two
  states: unanswered, the consent form; answered either way, the module.
  The gate tests ANSWERED, never the value: declining changes nothing about
  what the student does.

  There is no in-platform place to change the answer afterwards. This is a
  one-hour activity; a student who changes their mind tells the instructor,
  and the response is excluded downstream.

  The module itself stays launchable, so the same content serves outside a
  study with no wrapper at all. Which consent-form version a student saw is
  recoverable from the release the event log ties back to.
-->

<Vertical id="womens_sphere_study" title="READ 1000 — Women's Sphere (Research Study)" launchable="true">
<Use ref="womens_sphere_irb_consent_form" when="!@womens_sphere_irb_consent.value" />
<Use ref="womens_sphere_module"       when="@womens_sphere_irb_consent.value" />

<!-- The form is defined here unrendered and shown through the <Use> above,
     so its state has one home. Bracketed text is the IRB protocol's; it is
     replaced verbatim from the approved protocol before students arrive. -->
<Hidden id="womens_sphere_consent_defs">
<Vertical id="womens_sphere_irb_consent_form" title="Research Consent">
<Markdown id="womens_sphere_irb_consent_text">
# Middle Tennessee State University

## Informed Consent

**Title:** [Study title from the IRB protocol]

**Principal Investigator:** [Name, department, MTSU]

**Contact:** [PI email and phone]

## What this is

You are being asked to take part in a research study about how students
read and reason with college texts. The study uses the READ 1000 reading
module you are about to complete. Whether or not you take part, the module
is the same, and it counts for READ 1000 in the same way.

## What we would use

If you agree, your responses in this module — your answers, highlights, and
writing — may be included in the research after the semester ends. They are
stored under a study username, not your name. Your instructor and TAs will
not know whether you agreed until after grades are submitted.

## Voluntary

Taking part is voluntary. Saying no has no effect on your grade or your
standing in READ 1000. If you later change your mind, tell your instructor,
and your responses will be left out.

## Your choice

Please choose one. Either answer takes you into the module.
</Markdown>
<ChoiceInput id="womens_sphere_irb_consent">
  <Key id="womens_sphere_irb_consent_consented" value="consented"> I agree to take part in the study.       </Key>
  <Key id="womens_sphere_irb_consent_declined"  value="declined" > I do not want to take part in the study. </Key>
</ChoiceInput>
</Vertical> <!-- womens_sphere_irb_consent_form -->
</Hidden>
</Vertical> <!-- womens_sphere_study -->
